2.1. Application to Storm Surge Decision Making
\par
The network framework proposed here can pro-
\par
vide a basis for exploring the broader dimensions of
\par
VOI for decision aids. We are currently undertaking
\par
a study in which the various dimensions of VOI for
\par
a decision aid of coastal storm surge flooding will be
\par
examined in an integrated, interdisciplinary manner.
\par
The ongoing study considers the: (i) level of
\par
uncertainty that a fully informed scientific expert
\par
would have, due to the rarity of events, the incom-
\par
plete historical record, and uncertain future trends
\par
in storm occurrence and baseline sea level; (ii) prior
\par
knowledge, beliefs, and preferences of current and
\par
potential coastal homeowners; and (iii) change in
\par
knowledge, beliefs, and preferences as a result of
\par
exposure to (different versions of) a decision aid.
\par
The study involves an interdisciplinary team address-
\par
ing the science and statistics of coastal flooding, as
\par
well as social and behavioral scientists skilled in the
\par
cognitive and affective elements of risk perception.
\par
The study will employ traditional measures of VOI
