V. SIMULATION EXPERIMENTS
\par
In this section, we investigate the impacts of TSC, INS, and
\par
VMI on the occurrences of bankruptcy through agent-based sim-
\par
ulation experiments. The simulation experiments are designed
\par
and implemented on the Swarm platform. Swarm is a multiagent
\par
simulation platform designed by Santa Fe Institute for studying
\par
complex adaptive system (CAS), which has been shown to be
\par
effective in its applications in the fields of supply chain manage-
\par
ment (e.g., [33] and [34]). We next briefly describe the simula-
\par
tion model, and then, perform simulations under different sets
\par
of model parameters.
