1. Introduction
\par
Many freshwater ecosystems are currently jeopardized by
\par
human intrusion, without proper documentation of their base-
\par
line state and how humans have altered their biotic communities
\par
and biogeochemical cycles. The invasion of biotic communities by
\par
non-native species is perhaps the greatest threat to the integrity
\par
of lakes and rivers (Schindler, 2001). Climate-induced chemical
\par
and biological responses in lakes are another important issue,
\par
and several ecological and biogeochemical studies have shown a
\par
coupling among lake temperatures and water chemistry, individ-
