\par
Abstract: In recent years, the generation of a large amount of construction and demolition waste
\par
(CDW) has threatened the public environment and human health. The inefficient supply chain of
\par
CDW resource utilization hinders the green development of countries around the world, including
\par
China. This study aims to reveal the impact of information sharing regarding recyclers' market
\par
demand forecast on the performance of CDW resource utilization supply chains. Therefore, this
\par
paper uses the incomplete information dynamic game method to establish and solve the decision-
\par
making model of the construction and demolition waste resource utilization supply chain under the
\par
conditions of recyclers sharing and not sharing their information. The paper then obtains the Bayesian
\par
equilibrium solution and the optimal expected profit for each party. Finally, a numerical simulation
\par
was used in order to verify the validity of the model and conclusions. The main conclusions are as
\par
follows. In the CDW resource utilization supply chain, if the recycler is more pessimistic about the
\par
market's demand forecast, their information sharing makes the remanufacturer more motivated to
\par
improve their level of environmental responsibility. In addition, information sharing by recyclers is
\par
always beneficial in increasing the profit of the remanufacturer, but it also may make the recycler lose
\par
profit. When the efficiency of the environmental responsibility investment of remanufacturers is in a
\par
high range, information sharing increases the profits of recyclers. Conversely, information sharing has
\par
no significant effect on the profits of recyclers. The impact on the profits of the entire CDW resource
\par
utilization supply chain depends on the intensity of competition among channels, the market share
\par
of offline recycling channels and the efficiency of environmental responsibility investments.
\par
Keywords: supply chain performance; dual-channel reverse supply chain; construction and demolition
\par
waste (CDW); Stackelberg game; information sharing
