3.1. Model Assumptions
\par
(1) In this study, remanufacturers are the leaders of the Stackelberg game and the CDW
\par
recyclers are the followers in this game [40,41].
\par
(2) It is assumed that the common knowledge of the remanufacturer and recycler include
\par
the potential market demand a. In addition to the recycler's market demand forecast
\par
information f is their private information, the recycler has the right to decide whether
\par
to share this information with the remanufacturer. The rest of the information is also
\par
common knowledge for the remanufacturer and recycler [42,43].
\par
(3) This paper mainly examines the recycling pricing of recyclers and remanufacturers in
\par
the CDW resource utilization supply chain and does not consider the sales pricing
\par
of the remanufactured products. Therefore, separate from the CDW recycling prices
\par
pr, pm and {$\omega$} as decision variables, it is assumed that the market sales price of CDW
\par
remanufactured products is a constant p.
\par
(4) The CDW that is recovered by the remanufacturer through offline channels is fully
\par
provided by the recycler and all of the CDW that is recovered through any means can
\par
be used for remanufacturing [44,45]. There is no difference in quality between the
\par
remanufactured products that are produced by the remanufacturer using CDW and
\par
new products that are produced from the raw materials [42,46]; that is, the CDW that
\par
is recycled through dual channels does not affect the quality of offline new product
\par
construction materials. However, these remanufactured products are superior to new
\par
products in terms of their environmental and economic performance [47].
\par
(5) In the offline recycling channel, the recycler can recycle CDW through their well-
\par
established recycling network; in the online recycling channel, the remanufacturer
\par
can contact consumers in order for them to recycle their CDW through the Internet.Int. J. Environ. Res. Public Health 2022, 19, 3878 8 of 22
\par
Obviously, in the production and operation processes, neither the recycler nor the
\par
remanufacturer has a fixed cost input. Therefore, this study does not consider the
\par
fixed costs of the recycler and the remanufacturer.
\par
